<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/</link><lastBuildDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 21:38:49 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Trump promised a 'Golden Age'. What has he delivered at home?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261103-trump-promised-a-golden-age-what-has-he-delivered-at-home</link><description>
Donald Trump promised Americans a “Golden Age” when he returned to the White House in January 2025. Since then, his administration has slashed government spending through DOGE, ramped up mass deportations, expanded ICE operations and pursued an aggressive crackdown on DEI programmes and transgender rights. But how much has he actually achieved, and at what cost? Vedika Bahl examines Trump's domestic agenda since returning to office.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/062b0288-d7c9-11f1-8d33-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/domestic-policy.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/062b0288-d7c9-11f1-8d33-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/domestic-policy.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1815b358-d7c9-11f1-ad2c-2b007ce09517</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 20:56:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Trickle or tsunami? Democrats eye gains in US midterm elections</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261103-trickle-or-tsunami-democrats-eye-gains-in-us-midterm-elections</link><description>
Will it be a trickle, a wave, or a tsunami? Election Day in the United States with Democrats hoping to take back one or both houses of Congress. We’ll track the turnout, gauge the mood and raise the curtain ahead of Midterms results that are sure to shape the last two years of Donald Trump’s second and final term. Will a US president who’s already broken norms with his maximum use of executive powers be affected by the results a little, a lot, or not at all? 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/41f61bb0-d7b8-11f1-95c1-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-03T181429Z-313567485-RC2HGOA1QIDG-RTRMADP-3-USA-ELECTION-FLORIDA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/41f61bb0-d7b8-11f1-95c1-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-03T181429Z-313567485-RC2HGOA1QIDG-RTRMADP-3-USA-ELECTION-FLORIDA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7ed90926-d7b7-11f1-8403-23dceba682b2</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 19:18:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Family wealth, Epstein, ‘vanity projects’: How Democrats plan to investigate Trump after midterms</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-trump-family-wealth-epstein-vanity-projects-democrats-plan-to-investigate-after-midterms</link><description>
Democrats are preparing to launch a flurry of investigations into President Donald Trump’s administration and business dealings if they retake one or both chambers of Congress, devising strategies to circumvent obstruction from the White House and avoid the impeachment deadlock that consumed the US legislature during Trump’s first term in office.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cc781a30-d7a0-11f1-bb6c-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26057665262358.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cc781a30-d7a0-11f1-bb6c-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26057665262358.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3864e1f8-d79f-11f1-bdfb-d161c0a57435</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 17:30:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cc781a30-d7a0-11f1-bb6c-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26057665262358.jpg">© J. Scott Applewhite, AP</source><dc:creator>Benjamin DODMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US Midterms: Texas Democrat Talarico holds last rally ahead of vote</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-texas-democrat-talarico-holds-last-rally-ahead-of-vote</link><description>
Texas Democratic nominee James Talarico held a final rally Monday ahead of US midterm elections on November 3. His race against Republican Ken Paxton could determine which party holds a majority in the Senate. If Talarico wins, it will be the first time a Texas Senate seat's turned blue since 1988.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d4db8858-d7a3-11f1-96d0-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/titre-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d4db8858-d7a3-11f1-96d0-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/titre-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">08869bfc-d7a4-11f1-8efb-13798a91479a</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 16:50:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US midterm elections: Over 58 million Americans cast early ballots</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterm-elections-over-58-million-americans-cast-early-ballots</link><description>
How powerful is US President Donald Trump? That’s the question pollsters have been asking in the lead-up to the midterm elections. Polls have opened in dozens of US states in what is widely considered a referendum on Donald Trump. Most polls suggest Democrats will take back the House of Representatives, but could they also take the Senate and stymie Trump’s agenda during his final two years in office?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ae1260dc-d7a0-11f1-9e64-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-0b76c009.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ae1260dc-d7a0-11f1-9e64-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-0b76c009.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7e0a4284-d79f-11f1-b24a-a30672f9c6f8</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 16:46:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US midterms: Talarico seeks to break Democrats' 30-year losing streak in Texas</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-talarico-seeks-to-break-democrats-30-year-losing-streak-in-texas</link><description>
In Texas, Democratic candidate James Talarico is leading the polls ahead of a high-stakes US Senate race against Republican Ken Paxton. The contest is one of the most closely watched battles of the midterm elections, with Democrats hoping to end a 30-year losing streak in the state. FRANCE 24's Andrés Espinal reports from Austin, Texas.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/083946e6-d7a3-11f1-a8e3-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-b7d619cc.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/083946e6-d7a3-11f1-a8e3-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-b7d619cc.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2b528f18-d7a1-11f1-a96c-79df773713c0</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 16:45:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Election officials brace for possible Trump interference in the midterms</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-how-state-officials-prepared-for-possible-trump-interference-in-the-midterms</link><description>
State officials who run US elections braced for possible intervention by President Donald Trump's administration in Tuesday's midterms, fearing federal authorities loyal to the president could disrupt voting, challenge ballot counts or try to block the certification of unfavorable results.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/75b70602-d7a5-11f1-97ab-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/bc104701a09f9c505036ada5a600528ca70ddfea.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/75b70602-d7a5-11f1-97ab-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/bc104701a09f9c505036ada5a600528ca70ddfea.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">76a9b32a-d7a5-11f1-81cf-3fa7a5f65f00</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 16:41:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/75b70602-d7a5-11f1-97ab-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/bc104701a09f9c505036ada5a600528ca70ddfea.jpg">© Brendan Smialowski / AFP/File</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Brazil keeps a close eye on US midterm elections</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-brazil-keeps-a-close-eye-on-us-midterm-elections</link><description>
Brazil is keeping a close eye on the US midterm elections. Since Donald Trump's return to the White House, relations between Brasilia and Washington have grown increasingly tense. On the economic front, aggressive trade policies have subjected Brazilian imports to some of the steepest tariffs globally, exacerbating friction with the Trump administration. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Rio de Janeiro Jan Onoszko has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dcee6d6c-d7a3-11f1-8c64-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-dd5dbc4b.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dcee6d6c-d7a3-11f1-8c64-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-dd5dbc4b.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">123e3840-d7a3-11f1-986b-4307ec9c2d2e</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 16:36:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump focused on 'what's important to him': 'Tone-deaf for a normally shrewd populist operator'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/trump-focused-on-what-s-important-to-him-tone-deaf-for-a-normally-shrewd-populist-operator</link><description>
Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Doug Heye, Republican strategist, founder of Douglas Media, and former Communications Director for the Republican National Committee (RNC). As Americans head to the polls, Republicans face a challenge that goes beyond the familiar electoral backlash against an incumbent president. For Heye, Donald Trump's greatest political vulnerability may lie in the widening gap between his rhetoric of economic success and voters' everyday financial anxieties. "For a lot of voters, they see him focused on what's important to him, not what's important to them," Heye explains. Yet he also cautions against interpreting Democratic gains as a sign of renewed confidence in the opposition. Rather than a resurgence of partisan enthusiasm, the elections may expose an electorate increasingly disillusioned with both parties.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a936c1f8-d79a-11f1-927d-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261103-151032-152110-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a936c1f8-d79a-11f1-927d-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261103-151032-152110-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ae6db88e-d79a-11f1-9a41-c3d6717c833f</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 16:05:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US midterms: Michigan Senate candidate El-Sayed becomes Democrats' rising star</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-michigan-senate-candidate-el-sayed-becomes-democrats-rising-star</link><description>
In the US midterm elections, Democrat Abdul El-Sayed and Republican Mike Rogers are testing two sharply different strategies to win over voters in one of the nation's premier swing states on Tuesday, November 3, in a closely watched race that could determine control of the Senate. Progressive candidate El-Sayed has so far outpolled his Republican rival and is emerging as one of the Democratic Party's rising stars.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8f73e3a-d798-11f1-8d1b-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-03T021915Z-175384172-RC21GOAL3HUT-RTRMADP-3-USA-ELECTION-MICHIGAN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8f73e3a-d798-11f1-8d1b-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-03T021915Z-175384172-RC21GOAL3HUT-RTRMADP-3-USA-ELECTION-MICHIGAN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e6139c40-d795-11f1-a05a-b99ef6dd7b26</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 15:41:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US midterms: Michigan candidate El-Sayed pledges to tackle the affordability crisis</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-michigan-candidate-el-sayed-pledges-to-tackle-the-affordability-crisis</link><description>
The cost of living is one of the main concerns for many US voters as the midterm elections get underway. In Michigan, Democratic Senate candidate Abdul El-Sayed has pledged to "take the money out of politics and put it in your pocket", as FRANCE 24 correspondent Jessica Le Masurier reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/86b7508a-d799-11f1-ac61-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-24e76c03.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/86b7508a-d799-11f1-ac61-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-24e76c03.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ddeb91b0-d797-11f1-95e6-cf155bf49add</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 15:34:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Your donut, your vote': Texas group uses free food to attract young voters</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-your-donut-your-vote-texas-group-uses-free-food-to-attract-young-voters</link><description>
US voters on Tuesday headed to the polls in midterm elections that could shape the political future of the country. But navigating the voting process can sometimes discourage voters – particularly younger ones. In Texas, an organisation reached out to them directly by handing out free food, to then help them overcome these obstacles. FRANCE 24's Special envoy Tarek Kai reports from Austin. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ff05cc8c-d790-11f1-a95a-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8705fe98.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ff05cc8c-d790-11f1-a95a-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8705fe98.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">75d1b972-d78f-11f1-8419-a7b99722fd37</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 15:26:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Entre Nous</category><title>Political parallels in France and the US: Anger at the ballot box and in the streets</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261103-political-parallels-in-france-and-us-anger-at-the-ballot-box-and-in-the-streets</link><description>
Anger has long been a driving force for political change, but with the midterm elections in the US and the ongoing protests in France, widespread anger in both nations is currently front and centre. We take a look at some of the common issues causing this anger on both sides of the Atlantic, including the rising cost of living, a loss of faith in institutions and an eroding of the social contract. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c1bfa7e-d78f-11f1-a058-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-667ff99f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c1bfa7e-d78f-11f1-a058-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-667ff99f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9e966c42-d78d-11f1-800f-797807b5100c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 15:21:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Solange MOUGIN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US midterms: All eyes on crucial Michigan Senate race</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-all-eyes-on-crucial-michigan-senate-race</link><description>
In the US midterm elections, the Senate race in Michigan has been one of the most closely watched in the country. It took an unexpected turn on Sunday after Democratic Congresswoman Haley Stevens endorsed Republican Mike Rogers over Democratic nominee Abdul El-Sayed. Both candidates made their final pitches to voters during campaign rallies on Monday evening, November 2. FRANCE 24's Jessica Le Masurier reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f194c78c-d791-11f1-8a10-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-ec985e87.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f194c78c-d791-11f1-8a10-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-ec985e87.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bc66656c-d790-11f1-8181-77a18b1366df</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 15:15:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US midterm elections: A referendum on President Donald Trump?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterm-elections-a-referendum-on-president-donald-trump</link><description>
Americans deliver their verdict on Donald Trump's tumultuous first term in midterm elections that threaten to shatter his grip on Washington, with Democrats poised to seize the House and within striking distance of the Senate.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/87057ba4-d779-11f1-a078-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-07859cae.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/87057ba4-d779-11f1-a078-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-07859cae.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">054de1e2-d778-11f1-8c91-1731a2a44c48</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 13:56:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US Supreme court rejects Trump request to set aside 20,000 California ballots</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-supreme-court-rejects-trump-request-to-set-aside-20-000-california-ballots</link><description>
The US Supreme Court rejected the Trump administration’s push to force California to set aside 20,000 ballots from people the federal government claims are noncitizens, a decision that came hours before the final day of voting in the pivotal midterm elections. FRANCE 24's correspondent Wassim Cornet reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/451554a6-d78a-11f1-8a9f-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7d06555a.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/451554a6-d78a-11f1-8a9f-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7d06555a.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6189e2ac-d779-11f1-aa27-813072c02d5d</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 13:27:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>What could happen if Donald Trump loses US midterm elections?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-what-could-happen-if-donald-trump-loses-us-midterm-elections</link><description>
Americans head to the polls on Tuesday in pivotal midterm elections, with Democrats hoping to seize control of Congress and impose the first significant checks on Donald Trump's second term in the White House. But what could happen in the United States if Republicans lose control of Congress? FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Philip Turle has more. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/29f7ba36-d77d-11f1-af13-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5031862c.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/29f7ba36-d77d-11f1-af13-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5031862c.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fce5bba6-d77c-11f1-bc81-23d19c741ad6</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 13:24:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US Midterms: Could a blue wave widen the centrist-progressive divide among Democrats ahead of 2028?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-could-a-blue-wave-widen-the-centrist-progressive-divide-among-democrats-ahead-of-2028</link><description>
As the US approaches the midterms, the contest is emerging as a referendum on Donald Trump, the resilience of American democratic institutions and the ability of a divided Democratic Party to transform widespread public dissatisfaction into a coherent political alternative. With some Republicans now seeking to distance themselves from Trump, Katy Hull, Assistant Professor of American Studies at the University of Amsterdam, suggests that the president's highly populist and personalised approach to politics is becoming an electoral liability. Philip Turle observes Republican voters turning towards the opposition "as a form of protest against Donald Trump", rather than an endorsement of the Democrats.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6434daaa-d785-11f1-ae71-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261103-131056-131736-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6434daaa-d785-11f1-ae71-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261103-131056-131736-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6936c73e-d785-11f1-81cb-f971b47ba0af</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 13:19:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US strikes Iran's Qeshm Island as midterm elections start</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-strikes-iran-s-qeshm-island-as-midterm-elections-start</link><description>
The United States has conducted defensive strikes on some Iranian targets in the Strait of Hormuz, a US official said Monday, on the eve of crucial midterm elections. The unpopular Iran war and the resulting impact on U.S. gasoline prices and other parts of the economy have been a vulnerability for Republicans as they try to keep control of Congress. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Oliver Farry has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1003a828-d774-11f1-9b94-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-9793ec23.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1003a828-d774-11f1-9b94-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-9793ec23.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e697f396-d772-11f1-987f-d558a1b20435</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 12:12:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>US midterm elections: Food stamp crisis a key campaign issue in Arizona</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261103-us-midterm-elections-food-stamp-crisis-a-key-campaign-issue-in-arizona</link><description>
Arizona, a battleground state in the US midterm elections, is at the centre of a sweeping overhaul of America's social safety net. Since US President Donald Trump's tax and spending law passed last year, about half of the state's food stamp recipients have lost their benefits – the steepest drop in the country. State officials now admit that some of them are probably still eligible, but the errors have caused food insecurity to spike. The fallout has become a key issue on the campaign trail.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1009890e-d77a-11f1-bf3b-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-2b89cc2f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1009890e-d77a-11f1-bf3b-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-2b89cc2f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">11029cae-d6e1-11f1-b584-3570d1abc161</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 11:35:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Pierrick LEURENT</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Midterms live: Voting under way to determine control of Congress and the future of Trump's agenda</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-live-americans-head-to-the-polls-to-vote-in-us-midterm-elections</link><description>
Americans vote Tuesday in midterm elections that will determine control of Congress and which are widely seen as a referendum on US President Donald Trump. Democrats are projected to win the three seats needed to retake control of the House, although regaining control of the Senate is far less certain. Follow our liveblog for all the latest. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/025b8dee-d7b5-11f1-ac80-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/Midterms-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/025b8dee-d7b5-11f1-ac80-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/Midterms-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dc914a3e-d711-11f1-86cb-bfbbcbd756b8</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 05:45:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/025b8dee-d7b5-11f1-ac80-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/Midterms-1.jpg">© Yuki Iwamura, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Trump promised 'no more wars'. His foreign policy tells another story</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261102-trump-promised-no-more-wars-his-foreign-policy-tells-another-story</link><description>
US President Donald Trump promised an "America First" foreign policy and pledged to keep the US out of foreign wars. But since returning to the White House, his administration has been deeply involved in conflicts around the world. From the war in Ukraine and threats towards Greenland and Canada, to the US intervention in Venezuela, to Trump's shifting approach to the Middle East and war with Iran, Vedika Bahl examines his foreign policy record since returning to office.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/67eb27a2-d6fa-11f1-8418-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1a252fd9.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/67eb27a2-d6fa-11f1-8418-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1a252fd9.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">24ae7466-d705-11f1-9b8a-d54c41a9e709</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 21:34:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Free and fair? The midterms and the state of US democracy</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261102-free-and-fair-the-midterms-and-the-state-of-us-democracy</link><description>
How far will the president of the United States press this time if Tuesday's midterm elections don't go his party's way? From "only if the Republicans win" campaign promises to a US Justice Department that's already got involved in races, will the White House weigh on the outcome? How will ballot counting go? What's changed since Donald Trump's "stop the steal" rhetoric led to the January 6, 2021 storming of the US Capitol?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c085514e-d6f0-11f1-8735-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-02T150455Z-57526818-RC29FOA6T5LS-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-ELECTION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c085514e-d6f0-11f1-8735-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-02T150455Z-57526818-RC29FOA6T5LS-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-ELECTION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f4c3dcec-d6ef-11f1-9ae5-e5117919b596</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 19:37:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>MAGA: Why are Trump's most loyal supporters turning against him?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/maga-why-trump-s-most-loyal-supporters-are-turning-against-him</link><description>
Is Trump losing the support of the very coalition that brought him back to power?
 
Just one day before the midterm elections, Trump's approval rating stands at 32%, one of the lowest ever recorded at this stage of a presidency.
 
And discontent is growing beyond Democratic voters. Some of Trump's most loyal Republican and MAGA supporters are increasingly torn between political loyalty and economic reality. The war in Iran, rising costs linked to the Strait of Hormuz blockade, unfulfilled “America First” promises and other controversial issues, including the Epstein files scandal, are widening the rift between Trump and his electoral base.
 
Can he regain control of the diverse coalition that makes up MAGA?
 
FRANCE 24 journalist Stella Elgersma spoke to MAGA and Republican experts to explore how the movement has evolved, what its supporters want and what is driving their discontent.
 
Watch the full youtube documentary : https://youtu.be/XkehRG77itY?si=iOfIl0PwrgyX-j0X
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e4a4e68e-d6f0-11f1-a46d-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/minia-2-3.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e4a4e68e-d6f0-11f1-a46d-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/minia-2-3.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1a78c37e-d6ed-11f1-b42b-d5308eebe08e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 19:17:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>What changes if Democrats win a majority in Congress?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261102-what-changes-if-democrats-win-a-majority-in-congress</link><description>
Americans head to the polls on Tuesday for the US midterm elections, which could flip the majority in one or both houses of Congress from the Republicans to the Democrats. What would a Democratic majority mean for the country's political landscape, and how might Democrats move to keep President Donald Trump in check?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d61f8930-c86c-11f1-ab9a-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/main-pouvoir-congres-democrate.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d61f8930-c86c-11f1-ab9a-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/main-pouvoir-congres-democrate.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ce5e5364-d6d3-11f1-805b-730585255cda</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 16:29:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d61f8930-c86c-11f1-ab9a-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/main-pouvoir-congres-democrate.jpg">© France Médias Monde Graphics Studio</source><dc:creator>Romain HOUEIX</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nine dead in small plane crash near Trump's Florida home</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-nine-dead-in-small-plane-crash-near-trump-s-florida-home</link><description>
Nine people were killed Sunday when the Learjet they were travelling in plummeted into a neighbourhood in southern Florida, just miles from US President Donald Trump's resort home of Mar-a-Lago, officials said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1373b412-d6cf-11f1-99ce-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/mini2-5.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1373b412-d6cf-11f1-99ce-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/mini2-5.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b016d92a-d6cf-11f1-9bcd-cb669b5f6870</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 15:33:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Heading into the midterms, 'no US president in recent times has been as unpopular as Donald Trump'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/heading-into-the-midterms-no-us-president-in-recent-times-has-been-as-unpopular-as-donald-trump</link><description>
Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Richard Johnson, Senior Lecturer in US Politics at Queen Mary University of London. He says that "Donald Trump is damaged goods at this point in his presidency." With this uncompromising assessment, Johnson takes us through the political forces shaping the 2026 US midterm elections. Far from assuming that Trump's formidable campaigning instincts can once again mobilize Republican voters, Johnson questions whether the president's political influence has become a liability for the very party he once transformed. He points to a potentially significant realignment within the American electorate. Economic grievances, rising living costs, trade disputes and disillusionment with the war in Iran appear, in Johnson's reading, to be weakening important elements of the coalition that sustained Trump's return to power. Particularly consequential is the possibility that Latino voters, agricultural communities and sections of the MAGA electorate may be reconsidering their political loyalties or withdrawing from electoral participation altogether.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bdbaa30e-d6cf-11f1-ab72-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261102-150111-151452-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bdbaa30e-d6cf-11f1-ab72-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261102-150111-151452-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c3190430-d6cf-11f1-96bf-b1807fb543aa</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 15:25:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US Midterms: Will Gen Z enthusiasm help turn Michigan Senate blue?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-us-midterms-will-gen-z-enthusiasm-help-turn-michigan-senate-blue</link><description>
Michigan’s Senate seat is a must-win for the Democratic Party as it seeks to take control of the upper house of Congress. There’s a surge of energy behind progressive candidate Abdul El-Sayed, especially among younger voters. But can Gen Z's enthusiasm translate into votes and help Democrats win a critical Senate seat?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4434a4ec-d6cc-11f1-94f1-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-815f4d3f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4434a4ec-d6cc-11f1-94f1-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-815f4d3f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">33801bc8-d6cb-11f1-b8df-272a86085fe5</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 15:03:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>US midterm elections: North Carolina farmers hit hard by inflation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261102-us-midterm-elections-north-carolina-farmers-hit-hard-by-inflation</link><description>
On the eve of the midterm elections, US President Donald Trump's unpopularity is impacting Republicans across the board. Many states with seats once considered Republican strongholds are now on shaky ground. One of them is North Carolina, a rural state where one in five jobs is tied to agriculture.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6dfd6204-d6be-11f1-ade0-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-cbd2a019.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6dfd6204-d6be-11f1-ade0-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-cbd2a019.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5fb826f6-d480-11f1-bc79-6b6f931b1085</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 13:13:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Fanny ALLARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Michigan Democrat's endorsement of Republican ruffles critical Senate race</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-michigan-democrat-s-endorsement-of-republican-ruffles-critical-senate-race-1</link><description>
